hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27654","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, he said: Haddathana Uthman, meaning Ibn Hakim, he said: Amr al-Ansari narrated to me from Umm Sulaym bint Milhan, who is the mother of Anas ibn Malik, that she heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: No two Muslims lose three children not reaching puberty except that Allah admits them to Paradise by the grace of Allah and His mercy toward them."
"27655","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, he said: Haddathana Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, he said: Haddathana Abu Salamah, from Umm Sulaym, she said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the house of Umm Salamah, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, what about the woman who sees in her dream what the man sees? Umm Salamah said: You have shamed the women. She said: Allah, mighty and majestic, is not shy of the truth. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever of you sees that, let her wash."
"27656","Haddathana Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ru'asi, he said: Haddathana Zuhayr, from Abd al-Karim, from al-Bara', son of the daughter of Anas, who is the son of Zayd, from Anas, he said: My mother narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her, and in her house was a hanging waterskin. She said: So he drank from the waterskin standing. She said: So I went to the mouth of the waterskin and cut it off."
"27657","Haddathana Hasan, meaning Ibn Musa, he said: Haddathana Zuhayr, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik, from Umm Sulaym, that she was with the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while a driver was driving them, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Anjashah, gently, your driving with the glass vessels."
"27658","Haddathana Affan, he said: Haddathana Wuhayb, he said: Haddathana Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, from Umm Sulaym, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to visit her and nap at her place, and she would spread for him a leather mat and he would nap at her place, and he sweated much, so she would gather his sweat and put it in perfume and bottles. She said: And he used to pray upon the khumrah."
"27659","Haddathana Abu al-Mughirah, he said: Haddathana al-Awza'i, he said: Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah al-Ansari narrated to me from his grandmother Umm Sulaym, she said: She was neighboring Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she would enter upon her, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered, so Umm Sulaym said: O Messenger of Allah, what if the woman sees that her husband has intercourse with her in a dream, should she wash? So Umm Salamah said: May your hands be dusty, O Umm Sulaym, you have shamed the women before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So Umm Sulaym said: Allah is not shy of the truth, and if we ask the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about what is unclear to us, it is better than to be blind about it. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Umm Salamah: Rather you, may your hands be dusty. Yes, O Umm Sulaym, upon her is washing when she finds water. So Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of Allah, does the woman have water? So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: How else does her child resemble her? They are the counterparts of men."
"27660","Haddathana Affan: Haddathana Wuhayb, he said: Haddathana Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, from Umm Sulaym, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray upon the khumrah."
"27972","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating, from Anas ibn Malik, from Umm Sulaym, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, Anas is your servant; supplicate Allah for him. He said: He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, increase his wealth and his children, and bless him in what You have given him. Hajjaj said in his hadith: He said: Anas said: One of my children informed me that there was buried of my children and the children of my children more than a hundred."
"27973","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Rawh, the meaning, said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, that there was between Ibn Abbas and Zayd ibn Thabit a dispute concerning the woman who menstruates after she circumambulates the House on the day of sacrifice, regarding that. Zayd said: She shall not depart until her last covenant is with the House. And Ibn Abbas said: When she circumambulates on the day of sacrifice and becomes lawful to her husband, she may depart if she wishes, and need not wait. The Ansar said: O Ibn Abbas, if you oppose Zayd, we shall not follow you. Ibn Abbas said: Ask Umm Sulaym. So they asked her about that, and she informed that Safiyyah bint Huyayy ibn Akhtab was afflicted with that, and Aishah said: Wretchedness to you; you have detained us. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he ordered her to depart. And Umm Sulaym informed that she met with that, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered her to depart."
"27974","Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, and Rawh: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Karim informed me that al-Bara ibn Zayd, the son of the daughter of Anas ibn Malik, informed him that Anas ibn Malik narrates, from Umm Anas ibn Malik, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon us, with a waterskin hanging therein water, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drank standing from the mouth of the waterskin. So Umm Sulaym stood to the mouth of the waterskin and cut it off."
"27975","Yala and Muhammad said: Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Amr al-Ansari, from Umm Sulaym bint Milhan, she being the mother of Anas ibn Malik, Muhammad said: he informed him, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There are no two Muslims whose three children die before puberty, except Allah shall admit them to Paradise by the bounty of His mercy. He said it three times. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, and two. He said: And two."
"27976","Abu Kamil narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abd al-Karim al-Jazari narrated to us, from al-Bara, the son of the daughter of Anas, from Anas, from his mother, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered, with a waterskin hanging in the house, and drank from it standing. So I cut off its mouth, and it is indeed with me."
"27977","Rawh narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: And Ikrimah ibn Khalid said, from Zayd and Ibn Abbas: Ibn Abbas said to Zayd: Then ask your women, Umm Sulaym and her companions, did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, command them. So Zayd asked them, and they said: Yes, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us that."
"27978","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, he said: Zayd ibn Thabit and Ibn Abbas differed concerning the woman who menstruates after the visitation, on the day of sacrifice, after she circumambulated the House. Zayd said: Her last covenant shall be circumambulation of the House. And Ibn Abbas said: She may depart if she wishes. The Ansar said: We shall not follow you, O Ibn Abbas, while you oppose Zayd. And he said: Ask your companion Umm Sulaym. She said: I menstruated after I circumambulated the House on the day of sacrifice, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered me to depart. And Safiyyah menstruated, and Aishah said to her: Wretchedness to you; you shall detain us. That was mentioned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Order her to depart."
